* riskdep Monte Carlo
** Inputs (priors.py)
*** One prior per layer
*** p_year -> horizon probability
*** Beta severity, recovery
*** Basis in registry.json
** Draws (simulate.run)
*** 20,000 paths, seed 7
*** Bernoulli occurrence per layer
*** Beta severity per layer
*** D12: issuer hack forces a depeg
** One path (propagate.loss)
*** True value vs oracle value
*** Liquidation: oracle x LLTV < debt
*** Limited liability
** Outputs
*** Expected loss, P(loss), P(liquidation)
*** VaR / CVaR at 95 % and 99 %
*** Attribution: 4,000 draws per layer
*** Interaction term
left side
** Decision (decide.verdict)
*** Carry vs expected loss vs exit cost
*** Tail budget on CVaR 99 %
*** De-lever rerun, same seed
*** Oracle-sensitivity rerun
*** Risk multiple to exit
** Assumptions
*** Independent layers
*** Fixed priors
*** Incidents only
*** One position
** Planned
*** Incident mode, book, breakeven
*** Rates and implied yield
*** Common shock, cascade
*** Uncertain priors
@endmindmap
